---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy — The Fuel Pulse" description="Privacy Policy for thefuelpulse.com — how we handle data, cookies, and advertising.">
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto" data-reveal>

    <a href="/" class="text-xs text-base-content/40 hover:text-primary transition-colors mb-3 inline-block">← Back to dashboard</a>
    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold mb-2">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-base-content/40 mb-8">Last updated: April 2026</p>

    <div class="card bg-base-100 border border-base-300 p-6 md:p-8 space-y-8 text-base-content/70 leading-relaxed">

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-base-content mb-3">1. Who We Are</h2>
        <p>
          This Privacy Policy applies to <strong>The Fuel Pulse</strong>, accessible at
          <a href="https://thefuelpulse.com" class="link link-primary">thefuelpulse.com</a>.
          The site is operated as an independent fuel price information service covering Latvia.
          For privacy-related enquiries, contact us at
          <a href="mailto:info@thefuelpulse.com" class="link link-primary">info@thefuelpulse.com</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <div class="divider"></div>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-base-content mb-3">2. Information We Collect</h2>
        <p class="mb-3">
          The Fuel Pulse does <strong>not</strong> collect, store, or process any personally identifiable information.
          We do not have user accounts, registration forms, or comment systems.
        </p>
        <p>
          The only data processed on our servers is publicly available fuel price data scraped from retailer websites.
          No visitor data is retained on our infrastructure.
        </p>
      </section>

      <div class="divider"></div>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-base-content mb-3">3. Cookies</h2>
        <p class="mb-3">
          We store one first-party preference cookie:
        </p>
        <ul class="space-y-2 mb-3">
          <li class="flex gap-2">
            <span class="text-base-content/30 shrink-0 mt-1">›</span>
            <span><strong>fuel-theme</strong> — stores your light/dark theme preference in <code class="text-xs bg-base-200 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">localStorage</code>. This never leaves your device and is not transmitted to any server.</span>
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Third-party cookies may be set by Google AdSense (see Section 4). You can manage or block cookies through your browser settings or via
          <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="link link-primary">Google's Ads Settings</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <div class="divider"></div>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-base-content mb-3">4. Advertising — Google AdSense</h2>
        <p class="mb-3">
          This site uses <strong>Google AdSense</strong> to display advertisements. Google AdSense is operated by Google LLC,
          1600 Amphitheatre Parkway, Mountain View, CA 94043, USA.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-3">
          Google AdSense uses cookies and the DoubleClick cookie to serve ads based on your prior visits to this and other websites.
          These cookies allow Google and its partners to serve ads based on your visit to our site and/or other sites on the Internet.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-3">
          You may opt out of personalised advertising by visiting
          <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="link link-primary">Google's Ads Settings</a>
          or by visiting <a href="https://www.aboutads.info" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="link link-primary">aboutads.info</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          For more information about how Google uses data when you use our site, see
          <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="link link-primary">How Google uses data when you use our partners' sites or apps</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <div class="divider"></div>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-base-content mb-3">5. Third-Party Links</h2>
        <p>
          Our news feed and AI recommendations may contain links to external websites. We have no control over the content or
          privacy practices of those sites and are not responsible for their policies. We recommend reading the privacy policy
          of any external site you visit.
        </p>
      </section>

      <div class="divider"></div>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-base-content mb-3">6. Data Transfers</h2>
        <p>
          This site is hosted on Cloudflare's global edge network. By visiting the site, your request may be routed through
          Cloudflare servers outside the European Economic Area. Cloudflare's privacy practices are governed by the
          <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="link link-primary">Cloudflare Privacy Policy</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <div class="divider"></div>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-base-content mb-3">7. Children's Privacy</h2>
        <p>
          This site is not directed at children under 13 years of age. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children.
        </p>
      </section>

      <div class="divider"></div>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-base-content mb-3">8. Your Rights (GDPR)</h2>
        <p class="mb-3">
          If you are located in the European Economic Area, you have the right to access, correct, or delete any personal data
          we hold about you. As we do not collect personal data, there is nothing to access or delete on our side.
        </p>
        <p>
          For questions about your rights or to exercise them regarding Google's data collection, contact Google directly or
          use their
          <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/data-and-privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="link link-primary">Data & Privacy settings</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <div class="divider"></div>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-base-content mb-3">9. Changes to This Policy</h2>
        <p>
          We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Changes will be posted on this page with an updated date.
          Continued use of the site after any changes constitutes acceptance of the updated policy.
        </p>
      </section>

      <div class="divider"></div>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-base-content mb-3">10. Contact</h2>
        <p>
          For privacy-related questions or concerns, email us at
          <a href="mailto:info@thefuelpulse.com" class="link link-primary">info@thefuelpulse.com</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
